; Your velocity colour table, rebuilt from the picture of its colour bar: 25 swatches under 19 different numbers. Every swatch is a colour stop at its number and between two neighbouring
; swatches the colour runs in a straight line (in red, green and blue) from one to the other, so the table interpolates everywhere, whatever the bar looks like. Where a number has two swatches
; (-60, -10, 0, 10, 40, 80) the colour steps at that number: the first swatch's colour is the one just below it and the second swatch's the one from it upwards.
; Every colour is the swatch's own pixel value. Units: the numbers are taken as miles per hour (the three outermost, 224, 190 and 157, are 100, 85 and 70 m/s). Towards the radar is negative.
; Replace this file with the original .pal if you have it: the format is the same.
